urrent SOC after MISSION_05 turnaround + charge from charge_blocks. Let charge energy per block = 0.95 kWh (UAV_02 charge_kwh_per_block 0.95). So after k blocks, SOC = 2.573506 + k*0.95. Then after MISSION_01, SOC = that - 0.123506. Need >= 2.5. So 2.573506 - 0.123506 + k*0.95 >= 2.5 => 2.45 + k*0.95 >= 2.5 => k*0.95 >= 0.05 => k >= 0.0526, so k >= 1. So one charge block is enough. So we can set charge_blocks=1 for MISSION_05. Then charging occurs at slot 4 (since start at slot 4). MISSION_01 earliest departure would be after charging completes, i.e., after slot 4, so slot 5. But release slot 4, so depart at 5 is allowed. PATH_06 travel 1, arrival 6, due 18, fine. But need to check pad/charger capacities. MISSION_05 charging at VP_03 slot 4. Charger capacity at VP_03 is 2, so ok. Then MISSION_01 depart at 5, arrival 6. At VP_03, MISSION_01 departure at slot 5 uses a pad. But MISSION_05 turnaround was at 3, then charger at 4, so pad might be free. No conflict.\n\nBut also, note that MISSION_05 is urgent, and we are not holding it. So charge_blocks=1 for MISSION_05, depart 0, path PATH_01. MISSION_01 depart 5, path PATH_06, charge_blocks maybe 0? No further mission for UAV_02, so no need to charge after MISSION_01. So charge_blocks=0.\n\nNow check corridor closures for UAV_02: MISSION_05 PATH_01 uses COR_01 slots 0,1 (ok), MISSION_01 PATH_06 uses COR_02 slot 5 (depart 5, travel 1) so slot 5, COR_02 open. No corridor closures for them.\n\nNow check pad capacities at VP_03: MISSION_03 arrival 3 (UAV_01), turnaround 4; MISSION_05 arrival 2, turnaround 3; MISSION_01 departure 5. So overlapping: slot 3: MISSION_05 turnaround? Actually MISSION_05 turnaround is at slot 3, and MISSION_03 arrival at 3, and MISSION_03 turnaround at 4. So slot 3: one arrival (MISSION_03) and one turnaround (MISSION_05) -> pad usage: two pads used? Capacity 2, so ok. Slot 4: MISSION_03 turnaround, MISSION_05 charging (not pad), MISSION_01? MISSION_01 departure at 5. Slot 4 pad: MISSION_03 turnaro